{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975879-cardcaptor-sakura-as-minor-splat","id":975879,"title":"Cardcaptor Sakura as Minor Splat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-25T01:06:31-07:00","id":975879,"title":"Cardcaptor Sakura as Minor Splat?","content":"Okay, so, this is probably a bad idea, but hear me out; what if Cardcaptor Sakura were turned into a minor splat for the Chronicles of Darkness...or maybe a merit, like how Skinthieves were made for 2e (Dark Eras, if anyone's curious about where to find that)?<br /> <br /> Each card is a magical being created and bound into the form of a card, each card having their own powers for a particular use; these powers range from the fanciful (Flower creates flowers, Song duplicates the most beautiful singer's voice, Sweet makes things sweet or turns them into desserts), to the practical (Fly grants flight, Sleep causes people to fall asleep, Power grants extreme strength, Bubbles creates...cleaning bubbles) to the obscenely dangerous (Snow can bury an entire town in a constant, sentient snowstorm, Sword makes a weapon that can cut through almost anything and grants its user the knowledge in how to use it, and all the elemental cards can control the elements to a terrifying degree). Certain cards have more broad abilities, such as Shadow both being able to entrap things in cloak-like shadows and manipulate things through the user's shadow, but they all fall within a particular purview, and must be released from a sealed state in order to activate their abilities. Without direction/a master, they can cause a great deal of harm in the natural world. Some are malicious, many are mischievious, whereas some are gentle and have no desire to cause any harm, and they have their own sense of self. They were also created by a man who was not only extremely powerful, but he created such spirits often on whimsy (again, Bubble's main power is to clean things). If they weren't in a show with at most a pre-teen girl, this could very easily be turned into a horror series...then again, a young girl wielding the power to <br /> <br /> This sort of system has precident already in the form of Geist's Fetters, where a Ghost is bound to one of their Anchors and their most prominent/powerful is allowed to be used (albeit only once in a good while), and Mages proper have abilities that allow them to command spirits (albeit this is kind of an arm-twisting tactic) - I am fairly certain Werewolves also have a method of managing spirits, but I am not familiar with them (nor Mages for that matter). Is there a way that this could adapted to an ability mortals could wield, albeit one that required willpower to use and with a risk if they got free? I'm presuming people, even extremely powerful ones, cannot normally make Spirits (I did read some details about them, but they haven't stuck with me).<br /> <br /> I don't know, really. It seems like it could work, but I am far from an expert on the system and how to keep it balanced. Also it's 1am and I really shouldn't by typing this all out on an iPad...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:32:23-07:00","id":976028,"title":"","content":"Well, the escaped cards seem very much like spirits to me, and a Mage with 5 dots in the Spirit Arcanum can create spirits. Clow could easily have been a Mage. There's also a Spirit 4 spell that binds a spirit into an object, called a Fetish, that allows anyone who uses it (even a human) to activate a limited selection of the spirit's Influences and/or Numina (determined when the spell is cast). The Fetish is powered by the spirit's own Essence, and if the spirit gains enough Essence, it can escape. The sealed cards could be Fetishes. Mage also has something called Imbued Items, magical objects that store Mage spells and, like Fetishes, can be used by anyone including humans. They worki basically the same but are powered by Mana instead of Essence and there's no spirit to break free. The Sealing Wand could very well be an Imbued Item, imbued with the Craft Fetish spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-25-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:17:45-07:00","id":976041,"title":"","content":"Yeah, both Sakura and Shaoran seems like Proximi to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T12:42:39-07:00","id":976052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975879-cardcaptor-sakura-as-minor-splat?p=976028#post976028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the escaped cards seem very much like spirits to me, and a Mage with 5 dots in the Spirit Arcanum can create spirits. Clow could easily have been a Mage. There's also a Spirit 4 spell that binds a spirit into an object, called a Fetish, that allows anyone who uses it (even a human) to activate a limited selection of the spirit's Influences and/or Numina (determined when the spell is cast). The Fetish is powered by the spirit's own Essence, and if the spirit gains enough Essence, it can escape. The sealed cards could be Fetishes. Mage also has something called Imbued Items, magical objects that store Mage spells and, like Fetishes, can be used by anyone including humans. They worki basically the same but are powered by Mana instead of Essence and there's no spirit to break free. The Sealing Wand could very well be an Imbued Item, imbued with the Craft Fetish spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975879-cardcaptor-sakura-as-minor-splat?p=976041#post976041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, both Sakura and Shaoran seems like Proximi to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suddenly have a very vested interest in learning Mage. I probably won't be running any Cardcaptor games for a while, but this is still very encouraging. Thank you both for giving me this direction~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T23:36:35-07:00","id":976392,"title":"","content":"OK, so, there is one slight hiccough to this idea. In order for the imbued item to continue to work, it needs to be recharged with Mana. While this may not be a problem for a proximi, it would still mean that even with a bunch of points in battery the sealing wand would no longer work after a number of tries. Likewise, a mortal, or even a proximi, would have trouble finding places that would generate essence in the cards, if they even knew.<br /> <br /> Mind, you can always make them unique items, but right out of the box it is difficult.<br /> <br /> Also, made most of this with the iPod voice to text system, so I apologize for any errors. Manually editing what a gets wrong is a bit tricky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:48:37-07:00","id":976611,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sadly it's not perfect. You could maybe make the Sealing Wand an Artifact instead of an Imbued Item, with both Craft Fetish and Essence Fountain so it could refuel the Cards. And then it wouldn't need Mana to cast its spells either, though if the user did have the ability to fuel it with more mana that would be a bonus.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking, the wording of the Artifact Merit makes it seem like they can only be used by Awakened, but we could bend that rule a little bit in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:58:52-07:00","id":976726,"title":"","content":"That is a fair point; something I hadn't considered either was if there was a creature who served as a guardian of the cards who could work as a battery. Namely, Keroberos. While in the show, Kero was linked to Sakura's magic when she became master (as was Yue, which caused all sorts of problems), the the game he could be a unique creature, or even a Horror, recruited or created to guard the cards, and empower those who could collect them should they escape. Msybe Kero is connected to the collection, gaining more power for every card gained (Kero proper regained his powers with the collection of Firey and Earthy, so there is precident). It is something of a homebrew, but as you said Charlaquin, we could bend the rule a bit if one exists against this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:00:32-07:00","id":980046,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, I dislike double posting, but I just thought of something: if I were to make a bevy of spirits to act as the Cards, should I buy Werewolf: The Forsaken second edition in order to have a better idea on different spirits? Or is the core book (plus Mage: The Awakened second edition) good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}